    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d385">

                <pb facs="0705" n="569" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg569"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./589</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Guadeloupe</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hunt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guadeloupe</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-19">July 19, 1929</date>.<lb/>[Received August
                        6.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 72</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In acknowledgment of the Department’s
                    telegram of July 16th, regarding the flight of the Sikorsky Amphibian of the Pan
                    American Airways, a copy of which is enclosed herewith,<anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d385-f1"/> I have the honor to refer to my despatch No. 70 of July
                    5th, 1929,<anchor n="23" xml:id="d385-f2"/> and to report that following
                    telegrams from the Pan American Airways at San Juan, Porto Rico, announcing the
                    arrival of the Amphibian in Guadeloupe territory, a request for permission to
                    land was addressed to the Governor of the Colony on behalf of Mr. Robert G.
                    Thatch and his companions.</p>
                <p>The Governor refused to grant the authorization requested, on the grounds that
                    the request of Mr. Thatch was not received a sufficiently long time in advance
                    to allow him to take a decision in the matter.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Hunt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
